The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if (symlink(AFSDIR_SERVER_THISCELL_FILEPATH,
	    AFSDIR_CLIENT_THISCELL_FILEPATH))
	return errno;
if (symlink(AFSDIR_SERVER_CELLSERVDB_FILEPATH,
	    AFSDIR_CLIENT_CELLSERVDB_FILEPATH))
	return errno;
```
Reason:
The `bosserver` exits if the symlink creation fails, which occurs when the symlink already exists. This behavior prevents the server from restarting if the configuration files are already present, leading to an inability to use the `bos restart` command.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (symlink(AFSDIR_SERVER_THISCELL_FILEPATH,
	    AFSDIR_CLIENT_THISCELL_FILEPATH)) {
	if (errno != EEXIST) {
	    return errno;
	}
}
if (symlink(AFSDIR_SERVER_CELLSERVDB_FILEPATH,
	    AFSDIR_CLIENT_CELLSERVDB_FILEPATH)) {
	if (errno != EEXIST) {
	    return errno;
	}
}
```
Reason:
The patch modifies the symlink creation logic to check if the error is due to the symlink already existing (`EEXIST`). If it is, the function does not exit, allowing the server to continue running and enabling the `bos restart` command to work correctly.

